{"id":23009,"title":"Texture splats for 3D vector and scalar field visualization","url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/","final_url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/m2/1/high_res_d/10172798.pdf","year":1993,"kind":"paper","source":"openalex","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"59db3ec46c1d1056eebbcb3ee0eb402df4fae388e72a0c654254ae2614d68d8a","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1793063379.6983287,"text_chars":18221,"abstract":"Volume Visualization is becoming an important tool for understanding large 3D datasets. A popular technique for volume rendering is known as splatting. With new hardware architectures offering substantial improvements in the performance of rendering texture mapped objects, we present textured splats. An ideal reconstruction function for 3D signals is developed which can be used as a texture map for a splat. Extensions to the basic splatting technique are then developed to additionally represent vector fields.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/m2/1/high_res_d/10172798.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/","https://core.ac.uk/works/163029450","https://osti.gov/biblio/10172798","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/?q=volume splatting","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/?q=voxel engine","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/?q=3d texture based volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/?q=vector field volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/?q=3d texture volume rendering memory","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/?q=gaussian splatting","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/?q=tensor field visualization volume","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1339952/?q=footprint splatting volume rendering","http